ecause  he could have simply showed up and  played the fifth and said i can't talk  because i'm  the fifth amendment says i don't have to  incriminate myself right uh but trump  has sent a message he wants all of his  people to simply refuse to cooperate uh  that said the committee is hoping this  also sends a message to all of the other  people who they've subpoenaed who  haven't shown up yet because bannon has  the means to fight this he's a very  wealthy man other people in trump's  orbit do not have those resources so  we'll see how this plays out as soon as  he can i was going to ask you what  what's likely to happen next i mean he's  turned himself into the fbi what's the  likelihood that he will actually appear  before the house committee investigating  the january 6 attack  incredibly unlikely this is going to  take a while to work its way through the  court system uh so he's going to show up  before the magistrate today he's going  to be asked some questions told what his  rights are he'll  most likely plead not guilty and be  released uh to go home as this works its  way again these are misdemeanor counts  so the maximum penalty would be up to a  year in jail and a thousand dollar fine  so this obviously he's going to go to  trial if he's found guilty of contempt  let's say he's given probation or given  some jail time the committee can try to  subpoena him again they could go through  this whole process again but they can't  actually make him show up they can hold  him in contempt but they can't actually  make him show up and they certainly  can't make him testify because again the  fifth amendment he can simply say i  refuse to answer on the grounds that i  might incriminate myself all right patty  thank you very much for that patty cohen  live for us in washington  are you
 

